course: dictionary
lesson: 7747
title: Punctuate
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To punctuate means to put punctuation marks into writing, such as full stops, commas, question marks and speech marks. «A long sentence is not a run-on if it is punctuated properly.» Properly means with the right marks in the right places, so the reader can follow it.
explain: Punctuation marks are like road signs for the reader. A full stop says stop, a comma says pause for a breath, and speech marks show that someone is speaking. Check your writing by reading it aloud: wherever you naturally pause, you probably need a mark.
explain: The word can also mean to interrupt something again and again. «The speech was punctuated by cheers.» The cheers broke into the speech over and over. «Silence punctuated by drips» means the quiet was broken now and then by the sound of drips.
explain: Punctuate can also mean to stress a point. «He punctuated his words by banging the table.» The banging made his words stand out. It is the same word with three meanings, so check which one fits the sentence.
fact: Punctuate is a verb: punctuate, punctuates, punctuated, punctuating.
fact: To punctuate writing means to add marks such as full stops, commas, question marks and speech marks.
fact: «Punctuated by» can mean broken up now and then, as in «punctuated by cheers».
fact: To punctuate a point means to stress it, as in «he punctuated his words by banging the table».
fact: Speech marks, also called inverted commas, go round the words someone says.
exercise: Which mark should end this question: «Where are you going» | Exclamation mark (!) | Comma (,) | *Question mark (?) | Full stop (.)
exercise: Find the word that means broken up again and again: «The speech was punctuated by cheers.» | speech | was | cheers | *punctuated
exercise: What does punctuate mean in «He punctuated his words by banging the table»? | *To stress his words, so they stand out | To put commas into his words | To write his words down | To stop talking for a rest
test: Which of these is a punctuation mark? | Stress | Interrupt | *Comma | Verb
test: In «silence punctuated by drips», what does punctuated mean? | *Broken up now and then | Said loudly | Made into a question | Put in order
exam: Which sentence is punctuated correctly? | 'Wee eejit said Da | *'Wee eejit,' said Da. | wee eejit said da | Wee eejit, said Da
